{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And why were you afraid, etc.</b> Meaning: HaShem again presses the claim that they should have reasoned in their own minds that he stands and ministers before HaShem, and if he had done wrong HaShem would not have consented to work through him — say then, that in speaking against HaShem you spoke of one on whom He had consented to work. This is what He says: <b>why</b> etc., <b>against My servant</b>. And His saying <b>in Moses</b> means: a man who is distinguished as great in the eyes of HaShem — would you suspect him of something reprehensible? And it is possible that He further intimated to them by saying <b>in Moses</b> that they spoke to his face and shamed him with their words, as our Sages of blessed memory said, which I have written (Numbers 12:1)."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:08:06.535156641Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}